<title>USA: Berkshire Hathaway yr shr $2,065 vs $670.</title>
<headline>Berkshire Hathaway yr shr $2,065 vs $670.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, Neb. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996	     1995*</p>
<p> Earnings from operations    $  883.4	 $  669.9</p>
<p> Realized investment gain     1,605.2	    125.0</p>
<p> Net earnings		     2,488.6	    794.9</p>
<p>Average Class A equivalent</p>
<p>  shares outstanding	  1,205,257	1,187,102</p>
<p>Earnings per share</p>
<p>  Earnings from operations	  733		 564</p>
<p>  Net earnings			2,065		 670</p>
<p>(Dollar amounts in millions, except per share amounts) * Restated. On January 2, 1996, Berkshire completed the acquisition of about 49 percent of GEICO Insurance common stock not previously owned. In prior years Berkshire's investment in GEICO common had been carried at market value.</p>
<p>As a result of gaining control of GEICO in 1996, generally accepted accounting principles require that prior year results be restated to reflect Berkshire's prior investments in GEICO under the equity method.</p>
<p>Funn name Berkshire Hathaway Inc.</p>
</text>
